# Firebase Staging Deploy Guidance

The project has a permanent staging site on Firebase Hosting:
- Site ID: `reetle-staging-web`
- Permanent URL: `https://reetle-staging-web.web.app`

When deploying a staging version:

```bash
npm run build
firebase deploy --only hosting:staging
```

When deploying to production, always rebuild with the production API URL.
`.env.local` points at the staging API, so a plain `npm run build` produces a
site that talks to staging:

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://reetle-api-production-507485624349.us-central1.run.app/api npm run build
rg -l 'reetle-api-staging' out && echo "STOP: build points at staging" && exit 1
firebase deploy --only hosting:production
```

Never deploy a build made for staging to production, and never run a plain
`firebase deploy` (it deploys both the staging and production sites).
